 "brief": "# Build: notifications-control-panel\n\n## Brett said (verbatim)\n\"You need to have an administration panel. I need to control all the notifications. I need you to build a console control panel to enable and control all possible notifications.\"\n\nConsole plugin: one Notifications control panel.\n1. Inventory every notification source in console, AmberX, axHub (banners, alerts, approvals/veto, UI Review, builds, merge queue, CI, health checks, account/limits, Follow Amber, AmberX push). Report the list.\n2. One registry (notification types, source, channel). Every sender checks it before sending.\n3. Panel: per type on/off, channel (banner, AmberX push, sound, console pop-up), priority, quiet hours, test send; master switch; per app.\n4. REST + MCP + CLI so it can be set by voice.\n5. Coordinate with running build ui-review-notify-audio (UI Review push to AmberX): register its notification type here, don't rebuild it.\n6. Tests, README, screenshots to UI Review, PR to the merge queue. Do NOT land directly. Nothing removed. One session, lean chain.\n## Addendum 1 (Brett, voice)\n\"I need groups with commands with triggers with actions.\"\n- Notification groups (user-made, any types in a group, group on/off).\n- Triggers: rules for when a notification fires (event, conditions, thresholds, schedule).\n- Actions/commands: buttons on each notification that run a command (approve, open screen, run console command); custom commands per group.\n- All editable in the panel and via REST/MCP/CLI.\n",
